{"chars": "There is the North Pole Post Office, where letters from children all over the world arrive in big canvas sacks. The elves open every single one, read it carefully, and tuck it into a tall wall of wooden cubbies. The head of the post office is Juniper, who zooms between the cubbies in her wheelchair, its spokes painted like snowflakes, sorting letters faster than anyone else in the village. Whoosh, whoosh go the envelopes. There is the toy repair shop, where old, much-loved toys come to be mended: a teddy bear with a loose button eye, a wooden train with a wobbly wheel. The elf who mends them is Bob Mookie. He's tall for an elf and skinny as a candy cane, with a bushy white mustache that curls up at both ends, round spectacles perched on the tip of his nose, and a brown leather apron with pockets full of tiny screwdrivers and spools of thread. He has the biggest laugh in the whole village, a booming HA-HA-HOO that makes the toys on his shelves rattle. Once, just once, he went on vacation to a tropical island, and he has never stopped talking about it. If you ever smell pink guava cookies baking at the Gingerbread Oven, you can be sure Bob Mookie is somewhere nearby. And at the end of the lane stands a glass greenhouse that glows soft green in the dark. Inside it is warm and misty, full of plants from faraway places, and it belongs to someone you will meet very soon.", "start": [0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 0.375, 0.375, 0.375, 0.525, 0.525, 0.525, 0.525, 0.65, 0.65, 0.65, 0.65, 0.65, 0.65, 0.925, 0.925, 0.925, 0.925, 0.925, 1.262, 1.262, 1.262, 1.262, 1.262, 1.6, 1.6, 1.6, 1.6, 1.6, 1.6, 1.6, 2.3, 2.4, 2.4, 2.4, 2.4, 2.4, 2.4, 2.55, 2.55, 2.55, 2.55, 2.55, 2.55, 2.55, 2.55, 2.9, 2.9, 2.9, 2.9, 2.9, 3.112, 3.112, 3.112, 3.112, 3.112, 3.112, 3.112, 3.112, 3.112, 3.638, 3.638, 3.638, 3.638, 3.85, 3.85, 3.85, 3.85, 3.85, 4.075, 4.075, 4.075, 4.075, 4.175, 4.175, 4.175, 4.175, 4.175, 4.175, 4.45, 4.45, 4.45, 4.45, 4.45, 4.45, 4.45, 4.9, 4.9, 4.9, 5.062, 5.062,